Usage: snipe <command> [flags]

snipe: Go code navigation for Claude.

Notes:

    Start:      snipe index, then snipe context
    Flow:       context → pack <symbol> → callers/callees → tests <symbol>
    IDs chain:  every result's 'id' is valid input to the next command
    Index:      every command except search needs one
    Writes:     only edit modifies files; the rest are read-only

Flags:
  -h, --help                Show context-sensitive help.
      --limit=10            Cap results returned (applied after --select)
      --offset=0            Pagination offset
      --context=2           Context lines around match
      --no-body             Exclude function body
      --no-siblings         Exclude sibling declarations
      --signature-only      Return only signature (no body, no context)
      --max-tokens=0        Token budget (0 = unlimited)
      --format="concise"    concise (LLM default) | detailed | summary | json
                            (stable, for tooling) | human (TTY)
      --no-suggestions      Suppress next-step suggestions in Claude output
      --timeout=DURATION    Timeout for command (e.g., 30s, 5m)
      --select="all"        Pick top candidates by score: all, best, top3,
                            top5 (applied before --limit)

Orient:
  context    Start here — repo map: entry points, flows, boundaries
  orient     Write the full orient bundle to a directory

Navigate:
  def        Where a symbol is defined
  refs       Every reference to a symbol
  callers    Functions that call a symbol
  callees    Functions a symbol calls
  impl       Types that implement an interface
  tests      Tests that exercise a symbol

Read:
  show       Expand an id from any result
  sym        def + refs, callers, callees
  pack       sym + package role and purpose
  explain    pack + prose walkthrough and warnings
  pkg        Package overview and exported symbols

Find:
  search    Text search via ripgrep (no index needed)
  lits      Every location of a string literal or env var
  trace     A string literal with its call context
  sim       Semantic search (needs embeddings)

Change:
  impact       Blast radius of changing a symbol
  plan         Ordered edit worklist for changing a symbol
  risk         Risk verdict for a diff (base→head)
  verify       Minimal go test set for a diff
  triage       Facts for a file set: hotspots, package, tests
  sensitive    Files in security zones (auth, crypto, secrets)
  guard        Check architecture rules; exit non-zero on violation

Structure:
  deps         Package dependency graph
  importers    Files that import a package
  imports      Packages a file imports
  types        Type relationships
  boundary     Symbols whose refs cross two package sets
  lifecycle    Functions that create, mutate, read or delete a type
  hotspots     Files ranked by complexity × churn
  metrics      Graph metrics: PageRank, coupling, HITS
  deadcode     Exported symbols with no non-test refs
  c4           C4 facts: containers, datastores, flows

Views:
  diagram arch             Top packages by PageRank, grouped by layer
  diagram flow             Call graph from an entry symbol
  diagram lifecycle        CRUD groups for a type
  diagram seams            Interfaces ranked by implementations and fan-in
  diagram datastore-map    Each datastore's schema and reader/writer packages
  diagram system-map       Subsystems and the edges between them
  diagram class-map        Go types: fields, methods, embeds, implements
  report                   HTML dashboard for humans

Write:
  edit    AST-aware edit; dry-run unless --apply

System:
  index           Build or update the index
  status          Index freshness and counts (bare snipe)
  doctor          Diagnose install, config and index
  embed-status    Batch embedding job status
  version         Print version

Run "snipe <command> --help" for more information on a command.
